<div class="cover">
  <h1>ROCA NPD</h1>
  <div class="sub">End-to-End Code Review Guide</div>
  <p class="meta">New Product Development Request Tracker &nbsp;|&nbsp; Updated 25 September 2026 (Sprint 2 Complete) &nbsp;|&nbsp; SPFx + React + Redux + SharePoint</p>
</div>

<p>This document explains the complete ROCA NPD application for comprehensive code review: what each component is for, how it works, where data is fetched, which SharePoint lists own that data, how components connect through Redux and services, and the full request lifecycle from login to approval. It incorporates all Sprint 2 implementations, including the Vertical Head approval chain, MIS Coordinator actions, Other Details dynamic visibility, the dedicated <code>NPDApproverMail</code> webpart, the complete New Material Group module with Consultant SAP configuration flow, automatic lookup insertion, real-time lookup auto-refresh on navigation, dynamic <code>ActionVia</code> audit logging, empty Title column standards, and top SharePoint header layout accommodations.</p>

<h1>1. What this application is</h1>
<p>ROCA NPD is an enterprise SharePoint Framework (SPFx) client-side application suite consisting of two web parts: the main workbench (<b>NPD REQUESTS — New Product Development</b>) and the dedicated mail action receiver (<b>NPD APPROVER MAIL — Approval &amp; Action Handler</b>). Users create New Product Development requests and Material Group requests, save drafts, submit them into sequential approval workflows, and review requests across role-scoped dashboard screens. Administration of Lookup Types, Lookups, Workflow Configurations, and Brand Material Extensions lives in the same application.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>NPD Request Lifecycle:</b> Initiator Create / Save Draft / Submit → Vertical Head Approve / Rework / Reject → MIS Coordinator Other Details / Post to SAP / Approve.</li>
  <li><b>Material Group Lifecycle:</b> Initiator Category Selection / Multi-row Entry / Draft / Submit → Vertical Head Approve / Rework / Reject → Consultant SAP Configuration Note / Complete Request → Automatic creation of active entries in SharePoint <code>NPD_Lookup</code> list.</li>
  <li><b>Dedicated Mail Approval:</b> <code>NPDApproverMail</code> webpart processes actions directly from Outlook emails, featuring a centered dual concentric ring loader (inner rotating continuously, outer stationary), top-positioned status banners, token validation, duplicate action prevention, and <code>ActionVia = "Mail"</code> audit logging.</li>
  <li><b>Audit Logging Standard:</b> Dynamic <code>ActionVia</code> tracking (<b>Mail</b> vs <b>System</b>) across both <code>NPD_ApproversComments</code> and <code>NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</code>, displaying formatted date and time without hardcoding fallbacks.</li>
  <li><b>Title Column Standard:</b> <code>Title</code> column is strictly left empty for all list additions and drafts across <code>NPD_Request</code>, <code>NPD_ApproversComments</code>, and <code>NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</code>, preserving unique Request ID generation logic.</li>
  <li><b>Lookup Auto-Refresh on Navigation:</b> Navigation to components automatically re-fetches fresh lookup and brand options without requiring browser hard reloads.</li>
  <li><b>Layout &amp; Chrome Integration:</b> SharePoint default suite bar (profile, settings, app launcher) remains visible and accessible, with responsive height adjustments preserving clean UI positioning.</li>
</ul>

<h1>2. Technology stack</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th>Layer</th><th>Choice</th><th>Where it lives</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Host</td><td>SharePoint Online + SPFx 1.23.2</td><td>src/webparts/rocaNpd/RocaNpdWebPart.ts &amp; src/webparts/npdApproverMail/NpdApproverMailWebPart.ts</td></tr>
  <tr><td>UI</td><td>React 17 + PrimeReact 10, wrapped</td><td>components/common/controls/</td></tr>
  <tr><td>State</td><td>Redux Toolkit</td><td>src/store/ (slices &amp; thunks)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>SharePoint API</td><td>PnPjs v4 (spfi + SPFx)</td><td>External/CommonServices/SPServices.ts</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Routing</td><td>react-router-dom HashRouter</td><td>#/npd/..., #/mg/..., #/admin/...</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Styling</td><td>SCSS modules + theme.scss</td><td>External/CommonServices/theme.scss</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Standards</td><td>Mandatory MD docs</td><td>src/Documents/</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Feature screens must not import <code>primereact/*</code> directly; they use the common wrappers in <code>controls</code>. Components do not call SharePoint directly; they dispatch Redux thunks, thunks invoke business services, and services interact with SharePoint through <code>SPServices</code>.</p>

<h1>3. How the application starts</h1>
<p>Bootstrap is deterministic and unified. Application initialization does not re-instantiate PnP across components.</p>
<pre>RocaNpdWebPart.onInit / NpdApproverMailWebPart.onInit
  → loadApplicationStyles (PrimeReact theme + fonts + typography)
render
  → React.createElement(RocaNpd / NpdApproverMail, { context })
Component constructor
  → spfi().using(SPFx(context))
  → setupSP(sp) and setupSpfxContext(context)
  → &lt;Provider store&gt; → MainComponent / MailAppRoot
MainComponent
  → dispatch(initializeApp(spfxContext))
  → HashRouter → AppShell (Header + SideNavigation) → AppRoutes</pre>
<p><code>initializeApp</code> (src/store/thunks/appThunks.ts) writes user identity into <code>appSlice</code> (display name, email, login name, userId, site URL), then executes <code>resolveUserAccess</code> in <code>roleService.ts</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Adds Admin role if the user belongs to the NPD SharePoint group “Admins”.</li>
  <li>Queries ROCA master site <code>ApproversMaster</code> (expanding System, Role, Brand, Users).</li>
  <li>Matches the current user by email (using <code>normalizeEmail</code>) without guessing or filtering person fields via OData.</li>
  <li>Aggregates all matching roles into an access union (Initiator, Vertical Head, MIS Coordinator, Consultant) alongside brand permissions.</li>
  <li>Stores results in <code>appSlice.assignedRoles</code>, <code>mappedBrands</code>, <code>npdInitiatorBrands</code>, <code>npdVerticalHeadBrands</code>, and <code>mgRoles</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h1>4. Layered architecture &amp; Data flow</h1>
<pre>Screen / Layout Component
        ↓  dispatch(thunk) / useAppSelector(selector)
Redux Thunk (src/store/thunks)
        ↓  calls business logic
Service Layer (src/External/CommonServices)
        ↓  queries PnP via SPServices / Web([sp.web, rocaSiteUrl])
SharePoint List Items (NPD_Request, NPD_ItemDetails, NPD_ApproversComments, NPD_MaterialGroupRequests, NPD_Lookup)
        ↓  DTO mapping
Slice extraReducer updates Redux Store State
        ↓
Screen re-renders reactively</pre>

