<h1>8. Vertical Head — Approve, Reject, and Rework</h1>
<p>The Vertical Head (VH) approval flow is implemented end-to-end both from the application workbench and via Outlook email notifications.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Pending Queue:</b> VH navigates to <code>/npd/pending</code>. Requests are filtered strictly to brands mapped to the user in <code>ApproversMaster</code> for System = New Product Development and Role = Vertical Head.</li>
  <li><b>Form Action Mode:</b> Clicking Edit opens <code>/npd/new?id={Id}&amp;mode=edit&amp;from=pending</code>. General Information and Item Details are disabled (read-only). Footer mode resolves to Vertical Head actions: <b>Cancel / Back</b>, <b>Rework</b>, <b>Reject</b>, <b>Approve</b>.</li>
  <li><b>Remarks Validation:</b> Approver remarks are optional for Approve, but strictly mandatory for Rework and Reject (validated via <code>validateApproverRemarks</code> with immediate toast alerts).</li>
  <li><b>Approve Action:</b> Updates <code>WorkFlowJSON</code> step for Vertical Head to <code>Status = "Approved"</code> with comments and timestamp. Advances pending role to <code>MIS Coordinator</code>. Header <code>Status</code> remains <code>Pending</code>. Sends notification email to MIS Coordinator.</li>
  <li><b>Rework Action:</b> Updates <code>WorkFlowJSON</code> step to <code>Status = "Rework"</code>, sets header <code>Status = "Rework"</code>, and routes request back to Initiator's Draft / ReWork queue (<code>/npd/draft-rework</code>).</li>
  <li><b>Reject Action:</b> Updates <code>WorkFlowJSON</code> step to <code>Status = "Rejected"</code>, sets header <code>Status = "Rejected"</code>, and terminates workflow.</li>
  <li><b>Audit Logging:</b> Saves a new record to <code>NPD_ApproversComments</code> with <code>ApproverRole = "Vertical Head"</code>, <code>ActionVia = "System"</code> (or <code>"Mail"</code> if performed via email), <code>ActionOn</code> with full ISO timestamp (date + time), and <code>Title = ""</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h1>9. MIS Coordinator — Other Details &amp; Post to SAP</h1>
<p>The MIS Coordinator processes requests after Vertical Head approval, managing SAP master parameters and final approval.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Queue &amp; Brand Scope:</b> MIS Coordinator sees all requests pending at the MIS Coordinator step enterprise-wide (not brand-scoped, and not limited to the specific email in the JSON).</li>
  <li><b>Other Details Visibility Rule:</b>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Before Approved / Post to SAP:</b> The Other Details section is visible <b>ONLY to the MIS Coordinator</b> (hidden from Initiator and Vertical Head).</li>
      <li><b>After Approved / Post to SAP:</b> The Other Details section becomes visible to <b>EVERYONE</b> (Initiator, Vertical Head, and MIS Coordinator) in read-only view.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Field Auto-Population:</b>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Plant Code:</b> Automatically looked up from <code>PlantMaster</code> based on selected Material Type and Plant / Source.</li>
      <li><b>Profit Center:</b> Dropdown options dynamically loaded from active lookups (<code>NPD_Lookup</code>) via <code>fetchActiveLookups</code>.</li>
      <li><b>Material Extension:</b> Auto-populated from <code>NPD_BrandMaterialExtensionMaster</code> for the request's Brand.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Post to SAP / Approve:</b> MIS Coordinator verifies required SAP fields, enters remarks, and executes Post to SAP. The action updates <code>WorkFlowJSON</code> to Approved, transitions header <code>Status</code> to <b>Approved</b>, records audit log entry with <code>ActionVia = "System"</code> and empty Title, and moves request to <code>/npd/approved</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Rework / Reject:</b> Requires mandatory remarks, updating <code>WorkFlowJSON</code> and header status accordingly with audit log recording.</li>
</ul>

<h1>10. Dedicated NPDApproverMail Webpart</h1>
<p>The <code>NPDApproverMail</code> webpart provides a standalone, dedicated interface for handling approver actions clicked directly from Outlook emails.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Parameter Ingestion:</b> Reads query parameters: <code>requestId</code>, <code>action</code> (Approve, Rework, Reject), <code>token</code>, <code>approverEmail</code>, and <code>system</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Two-Ring Concentric Centered Loader:</b>
    <ul>
      <li>Positioned precisely at the <b>center of the viewport</b>.</li>
      <li>Features two visible concentric circular rings: the <b>inner circular ring rotates continuously</b>, while the <b>outer circular ring remains stationary</b>.</li>
      <li>Both rings are concurrently visible throughout processing.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Top-Positioned Alerts:</b> Normal success confirmation banners and already-submitted / already-acted alerts are positioned at the <b>top of the page</b>.</li>
  <li><b>Action Execution:</b> Validates token against <code>NPD_Request</code>. Executes workflow transition. Saves audit log to <code>NPD_ApproversComments</code> with <b><code>ActionVia = "Mail"</code></b>, complete date and time in <code>ActionOn</code>, and empty <code>Title</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Duplicate Action Prevention:</b> Re-clicking an email link after the step has already been processed immediately displays the top-level 'Already Submitted' informational banner without modifying list data.</li>
</ul>

<h1>11. New Material Group Module &amp; Consultant Flow</h1>
<p>The Material Group module is fully implemented for defining, submitting, approving, and configuring new material groups.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Master Category Cards:</b> Renders available categories (MG2 Product Group, MG3 Product Sub Group, MG4 Finish, MG5 Category, etc.) configured in <code>NPD_MaterialGroupConfigs</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Dynamic Table Grids:</b> Selecting categories dynamically renders input tables. Users can Add Row and Remove Row with validations for required Code, Description, and duplicate codes within categories.</li>
  <li><b>Save Draft &amp; Submit:</b>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Save Draft:</b> Writes partial entries to <code>NPD_MaterialGroupRequests</code> with <code>Status = "Draft"</code> and <code>Title = ""</code>. Appears in <code>/mg/draft-rework</code>.</li>
      <li><b>Submit Request:</b> Generates unique Request ID (MG-YYYY-####), writes request with <code>Status = "Pending"</code>, <code>Title = ""</code>, routes to Vertical Head, and sends notification email.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Vertical Head Flow:</b> MG Vertical Head reviews request in <code>/mg/new?id={Id}&amp;mode=edit&amp;from=pending</code>. Category entries are read-only. VH can Approve (routes to Consultant), Rework (returns to Initiator), or Reject. Writes audit log to <code>NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</code> with <code>ActionVia = "System"</code> and empty Title.</li>
  <li><b>Consultant SAP Configuration Flow:</b>
    <ul>
      <li>Consultant reviews pending requests at <code>/mg/pending</code>. Form renders dedicated <b>Consultant Remarks / SAP Configuration Note</b> panel.</li>
      <li>Consultant enters configuration notes and clicks Complete Request.</li>
      <li><b>Automatic Insertion into NPD_Lookup:</b> System automatically creates active records in the SharePoint <code>NPD_Lookup</code> list for every entry in the completed request, setting <code>Title = Description</code>, <code>LookupCode = Code</code>, <code>LookupTypeId = Category Id</code>, and <code>IsDeleted = "No"</code>.</li>
      <li>Status updates to <b>Completed</b>. Request moves to Completed Requests dashboard (<code>/mg/completed</code>).</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><b>Material Group Audit Log:</b> <code>MaterialGroupAuditLogTable</code> displays the complete audit history, including <code>ActionVia</code> ("System" or "Mail") and formatted date + time.</li>
</ul>

<h1>12. Lookup Auto-Refresh on Component Navigation</h1>
<p>To ensure that newly configured Material Groups and lookups are immediately available across the application without requiring a browser hard refresh (Ctrl+F5):</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Root Cause Addressed:</b> The Redux thunk <code>fetchNpdLookupOptions</code> previously contained a condition checking <code>Object.keys(form.lookupOptionsByType).length === 0</code>. After the initial page load, this condition returned false, aborting all subsequent fetch dispatches.</li>
  <li><b>Condition Fix:</b> Updated the thunk condition in <code>src/store/thunks/npdFormThunks.ts</code> to return <code>true</code> (skipping only when a request is currently in-flight with <code>status === "loading"</code>).</li>
  <li><b>Navigation Trigger:</b> In <code>useNpdRequestFormController.ts</code>, <code>useLocation()</code> is integrated with <code>location.key</code> and <code>location.pathname</code> in the <code>useEffect</code> dependencies. Navigating to New NPD Request (<code>/npd/new</code>) immediately triggers <code>dispatch(fetchNpdLookupOptions())</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Non-blocking UX:</b> If options are already loaded in memory, background re-fetching updates options seamlessly without flashing full-page blocking loaders.</li>
  <li><b>Common Applicability:</b> Also applied to brand options, Admin Lookup Master, Lookup Type Master, Brand Material Extension Master, Workflow Config Master, and Material Group Configs.</li>
</ul>

<h1>13. Audit Logging &amp; Title Column Standards</h1>
<table>
  <tr><th>Standard Area</th><th>Rule &amp; Implementation</th><th>Target Lists &amp; Components</th></tr>
  <tr><td>ActionVia Dynamic Tracking</td><td>Must record <code>ActionVia = "Mail"</code> when action occurs via Outlook / mail webpart; <code>ActionVia = "System"</code> when performed from application UI. Displayed dynamically in UI without hardcoding fallback.</td><td>NPD_ApproversComments, NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs, NpdAuditLogTable, MaterialGroupAuditLogTable</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ActionOn Full Timestamp</td><td>Stores complete ISO date and time. Formatted in UI as date and time (e.g. <code>DD/MM/YYYY HH:MM</code>).</td><td>NPD_ApproversComments, NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Title Column Left Empty</td><td>When items are created using <code>spAddItem</code> (including Drafts and audit rows), the <code>Title</code> column must be left empty (<code>""</code>). Do not store Brand in Title for drafts. Request ID generation logic operates independently.</td><td>NPD_Request, NPD_ApproversComments, NPD_MaterialGroupRequests, NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</td></tr>
  <tr><td>SharePoint Top Suite Bar</td><td>Default SharePoint top header (user profile, settings gear, app launcher) remains visible and unhidden. App header padding and margin adjusted for seamless vertical positioning.</td><td>hideSharePointChrome.ts, AppShell.module.scss</td></tr>
</table>

<h1>14. Suggested Code Review Checklist</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Review Workflow Logic:</b> Verify <code>npdWorkflowJsonService.ts</code> for correct role state transitions across Initiator, Vertical Head, and MIS Coordinator.</li>
  <li><b>Review Permission &amp; Visibility:</b> Verify <code>showOtherDetails</code> in <code>useNpdRequestFormController.ts</code> (MIS-only before approved; visible to everyone after approved).</li>
  <li><b>Review Mail Webpart:</b> Inspect <code>NpdApproverMail.tsx</code> and <code>NpdApproverMailLoader.tsx</code> for centered two-ring animation and top banner positioning.</li>
  <li><b>Review Material Group:</b> Check <code>useMaterialGroupFormController.ts</code> and <code>materialGroupThunks.ts</code> for category selection, validation, and auto-insertion into <code>NPD_Lookup</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Review Lookup Fetch Condition:</b> Check <code>npdFormThunks.ts</code> to ensure <code>fetchNpdLookupOptions</code> allows background navigation re-fetches.</li>
  <li><b>Review Audit Logging:</b> Verify <code>ActionVia</code> is dynamically set in <code>npdApproverCommentsService.ts</code> and <code>materialGroupAuditLogService.ts</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Review List Writes:</b> Confirm <code>Title</code> is passed as <code>""</code> in all <code>spAddItem</code> calls across <code>NPD_Request</code>, <code>NPD_ApproversComments</code>, and <code>NPD_MaterialGroupAuditLogs</code>.</li>
</ul>

